                  <provenance type="#b c" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_592">Winchester,
                        Hampshire. Abbey of St Mary the Virgin, of Benedictine nuns (Nunnaminster)</orgName><p>Written by a "scriptix". A note on fol. ii recto, written A. D.
                        1150, apparently concerns especially St Edburga (1st abbess of
                        Nunnaminster), whose name and King Alfred's are in capitals each time they
                        occur. </p><p>Medieval binding: the pastedowns are from monastic accounts A.
                        D. 1334 and include an item "pro petris de selborne" (for Selborne quarries
                        and their use for bindings at Winchester in the Middle Ages see V. C. H.
                        Hants., vol. 5). </p></provenance>
